Users (267 bankers, operations, SDC) access iTicket through a browser-based Angular 21 single-page application over secure HTTPS connections.
Requests pass through the Apigee API Gateway and PSG security gateway for authentication, rate limiting, and policy enforcement.
The OpenShift Route/Ingress terminates TLS and routes traffic to the appropriate deployable unit based on the request path.
Static frontend assets (Angular dist) are served by the Apache HTTP Server, which provides SSO support.
The Angular frontend invokes REST APIs exposed by the IBM WebSphere Liberty backend (Spring MVC / JAX-RS controllers).
The Liberty backend executes core deal-ticket business logic through Spring 7.x beans and EJB Session Beans, applying compliance and validation rules.
Persistence is handled by Hibernate 7.x (JPA), reading and writing to the Oracle 19c database via a JDBC connection pool.
Asynchronous integration with external systems (IPO, GTM, FXD, CRS, TPS, EMS, and others) flows through IBM MQ, consumed and produced by 14 message listeners.
Batch processing runs as Argo Workflows / OpenShift Jobs, handling feed checks, data uploads, report generation, and business date rollover.
Batch jobs exchange files with the on-premise NDM system via an SFTP bridge, while NDM itself remains on the VM.
Cross-cutting platform services provide secrets management (HashiCorp Vault, CyberArk), centralized logging (Kibana), application monitoring (AppDynamics), and externalized configuration (ConfigMaps)
